a creation unit, often 25,000 to 100,000 shares. Shares outstanding **increase** by that amount.\n- **Redemption:** When the price falls below NAV, an AP returns creation units to the fund and receives the underlying basket (or cash). Shares outstanding **decrease**.\n\nOrdinary secondary-market trades between investors don't change shares outstanding. They only transfer existing shares between buyers and sellers. This arbitrage process is what keeps the ETF's market price close to its NAV.","ttft_ms":1820,"type":"result","duration_ms":2965,"uuid":"a3992b4c-6281-41dd-b7ff-06e0d94a7c4b","ttft_stream_ms":438,"time_to_request_ms":66,"first_content_frame_ms":438,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
